WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.390
Episode four: resume the run and read its results.

2
00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:10.847
This video assumes APEX installed, as in episode one, and the run from episode three, stopped after two steps.

3
00:00:10.847 --> 00:00:16.597
Run every command below from the APEX folder.

4
00:00:16.597 --> 00:00:22.525
Every step is saved as a checkpoint in the run's folder.

5
00:00:22.525 --> 00:00:23.600
Now we resume it.

6
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:44.247
The run continues from its last checkpoint to the end; a resumed run gives exactly the same results as one that never stopped.

7
00:00:44.247 --> 00:00:46.535
What if we run the same command again?

8
00:00:46.535 --> 00:01:01.403
Running the same configuration again with apex run is refused while its folder holds a run.

9
00:01:01.403 --> 00:01:12.741
So: resume it, or give the new run another [run] name, here in the run section.

10
00:01:12.741 --> 00:01:41.524
The summary gives every metric at every step, as member means ± standard deviations (the sample standard deviation, so slightly larger than the run's table), from the prior (step 0) to the result.

11
00:01:41.524 --> 00:01:51.097
data_mismatch is what the method minimises: each member's misfit to the data, weighted by the data errors.

12
00:01:51.097 --> 00:01:58.150
normalized_data_mismatch is the mean square of the residuals to the observations, each scaled by its data error.

13
00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:05.384
Near 1, the members fit the data about as well as the data errors allow.

14
00:02:05.384 --> 00:02:13.343
rmse is the members' distance from the true model, which only a synthetic case has.

15
00:02:13.343 --> 00:02:19.677
model_change is how much the members changed in the last step.

16
00:02:19.677 --> 00:02:27.683
So: resume continues from the last checkpoint, with exactly the same results, and summary gives every metric at every step.

17
00:02:27.683 --> 00:02:33.767
In the next video: the figures, and a second method.

18
00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:39.267
Thank you for watching.
